WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.669
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.637
Let's get to the news
and jokes.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.573
Well, guys, after two days
of controversy,

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.909
today President Trump finally
did the right thing

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.978
and forcefully rejected
white supremacy.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.012
Take a look.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:14.247
[ Tone ]

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:20.754
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:21.754
I'm --

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.389
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.725
-I'm kidding.
He hasn't done that at all.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.027
And as a result, Republicans
are distancing themselves

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.529
from the president.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.697 line:0%
-The president's debate
performance has sparked

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:34.533 line:0%
a torrent of criticism
that even his most ardent allies

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.035 line:0%
have struggled to contain.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:37.737 line:0%
And Republicans on Capitol Hill

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.072 line:0%
are now distancing themselves
from the president

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:43.943 line:0%
after he failed to disavow
a far-right fascist group.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.278
-There's been six months
of a pandemic

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:48.248
and now the Republicans
are distancing?

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.649
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.150
Yup, they're really trying to
distance themselves

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.952
from Trump's
white supremacy issue.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.853
In fact, today Mitch McConnell
brought a bill

00:00:54.853 --> 00:00:57.790
to the Senate floor to bring
back the Source Awards.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.260
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.261
-Wait, what?

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:04.764
[ Applause ]

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.133
That's right, Republicans said
this as the last straw.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.268
Then tomorrow they'll be like,

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.003
"Oh, we found a bunch
more straws."

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.105
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.273
Turns out all these
controversies are causing

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.175
the president's biggest
supporters

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.211
to experience "Trump fatigue."

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.079
I think it might be true.
Today when Trump called in

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.714
to "Fox &amp; Friends,"
Steve Doocy was like,

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.016
"Ugh,
just let the machine get it."

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.517
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.286
"We have to talk for 45 minutes,
and just so --

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:28.821
Yeah, what did say?"

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:32.492
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.793
How do you get away from Trump
though?

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.160
It's like dealing with a bear.
Do you run?

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.529
Do you act big?
Do you play dead?

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.664
No one knows.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:40.166
That's right.
Republicans are finally

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.435
stepping up to say it's not okay
to publicly support

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:45.905
white supremacy...more than
seven or eight times, tops.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:49.242
Eight is -- eight is enough.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:53.145
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:55.482
Well, earlier today,
John Roberts from Fox News

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:58.150
tried to give the White House
a chance to clear things up

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.485
and denounce white supremacy,

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.587
but Press Secretary
Kayleigh McEnany

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:03.656
had a tough time with that.
Watch this.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:07.827 line:0%
-Just to clear it up this
morning, can you, naming it,

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.462 line:0%
make a declarative statement
that you denounce --

00:02:10.462 --> 00:02:12.431 line:0%
that the president denounces it?
-I just did.

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:13.866 line:0%
The president has denounced
this repeatedly.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:15.435 line:0%
-You read a bunch of quotes
from the past.

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:17.236 line:0%
-The president was asked this.
You're making --

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:19.038 line:0%
You're contriving a story.
-No I'm not.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:22.041
-Yeah, Trump's like
some sort of mythical troll.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.009
You got to ask the same question
three times before you

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:26.278
get the answer
you're looking for.

00:02:26.278 --> 00:02:30.383
[ With accent ] "There's only
one way to reveal the answer --

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.452
say the question,
but in reverse."

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:35.621
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:37.690
The only way their gonna condemn
white supremacy is

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.792
if you sneak it into Trump's
teleprompter the way you sneak

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.662
medicine into a dog food.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.897
[ As Trump ]
"And then we're gonna --

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.298
I do not support white
supremacists.

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:47.533
Bring back football."

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.802
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.537
After that exchange,
Roberts didn't hold back

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:52.638
how he was feeling.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:53.972
This is real.
Take a look at this.

00:02:53.972 --> 00:02:56.209 line:0%
-And for all of you
on Twitter who are hammering me

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.812 line:0%
for asking that question,
I don't care,

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:02.047 line:0%
because it's a question
that needs to be asked

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:04.716 line:0%
and clearly the president's
Republican colleagues

00:03:04.716 --> 00:03:06.352 line:0%
a mile away from here

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.554 line:0%
are looking for an answer
for it, too.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:13.426 line:0%
So stop deflecting.
Stop blaming the media.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.694 line:0%
I'm tired of it.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:17.864
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:22.368
[ Applause ]

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.404
-Even Fox News is fed up
with Trump.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:27.039
That's like HGTV telling
the Property Brothers

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.208
to take their tight jeans
and near beards and beat it.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:33.279
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.514
-Tariq: Near beards.

00:03:34.514 --> 00:03:36.549
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.051
[ Applause ]

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.787
-I hope that becomes a thing,
man.

00:03:41.787 --> 00:03:44.624
After Monday's tax bombshell,
Tuesday's debate debacle,

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.759
and Wednesday's
white supremacy disaster,

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.462
Trump seemed pretty down
at last night's rally.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:51.864
[ "YMCA" plays ]

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.499
-♪ Young man ♪

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:55.167
♪ There's no need to feel down ♪

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:58.438
♪ Stay at the YMCA ♪

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.273
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.608
-That's actual audio.
That's real -- yeah.

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:05.545
Yes, of course.
The classic "YMCA" dance.

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:08.714
Clapping, pointing, and drawing
a circle with you finger.

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:09.849
[ Laughter ]
One, two, three.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.383
It's fun to stay --

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.319
♪ YMCA ♪

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.920
♪♪

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.823
♪ YMCA ♪

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.525
♪ They got everything ♪

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:21.393
♪ Making boys to men ♪

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:25.031
♪ Everything that a man
could be ♪

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.233
♪♪

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.601
-Y...

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.270
Right after that dance,
white supremacists

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.406
forcefully rejected Trump.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.241
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.242
Here's a fun fact.
Trump is in so much debt

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:39.612
pretty soon he'll be staying
at the YMCA.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.147
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.215
After watching that, it's clear
that if the presidency

00:04:43.215 --> 00:04:46.619
doesn't work out, neither will
"Dancing With the Stars."

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.655
♪♪

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.190
I'm just kidding.
That was a nice moment.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.125
Trump was having fun.
The crowd was having fun.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:54.827
The coronavirus
was having fun.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.129
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.430
You know what, forget
the next debate.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:00.065
Let's just make it a dance-off
instead.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:01.634
-♪ Young man ♪

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.169
♪ When you're short on dough ♪

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:04.937
♪ You can stay there ♪

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.272
-Good God.

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:10.242
♪♪

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:13.112
[ Laughs ]

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.547
That's such a good move.

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:17.783
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.652
-Everyone is still
talking about the debates.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.687
Oh, my God. Well, except
for Rudy Giuliani,

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:23.623
who is talking
about the "debat."

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:26.292
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.993
Amazing, you can't even tweet
about the debate

00:05:27.993 --> 00:05:30.396
without Trump interrupting you.

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.198
Trump might be --
Rudy might be right, 'cause

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:35.534
I don't think you can legally
call what happened a debate.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.102
Not sure where Rudy was going
with this.

00:05:37.102 --> 00:05:38.937
He's either got something to say
about the debate

00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:41.640
or he's looking for
a D batteries.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.909
But Giuliani --

00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:45.111
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:49.615
♪♪

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:52.351
We are still on the air.
We are still on the air.

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:54.787
That's the good news.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.289
Actually, Giuliani quickly
noticed and followed that up

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:59.325
with a "Oops, my ba."

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:02.295
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:03.462
My ba.

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:06.732
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:09.135
Was afraid of the last letter.

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:10.536
-Yeah, I got it.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:14.173
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:17.843
The guy is doing Trump's debate
prep, he can't spell debate.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.679
That's like getting a text
from your surgeon that says,

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:21.581
"Can't wait for
your surjeree."

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.382
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:25.051
Some more news from Washington.
It just came out

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.785
that the White House
and the CDC

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:29.422
have been clashing over
how to handle cruise lines

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.190
during the pandemic,
take a look.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:35.694
-The CDC is extending its ban
on cruising from U.S. ports

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:37.529
through the end of this month.

00:06:37.529 --> 00:06:41.433
Axios is reporting the CDC's
director wanted to extend

00:06:41.433 --> 00:06:43.202
the order until February,

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:46.505
but Vice President Pence
overruled him.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:48.774
Even the cruise ships know
it's a bad idea.

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:51.477
For a six-day trip they tell
you to pack for nine months.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:54.480
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.149
It'll be a while.

00:06:56.149 --> 00:06:58.417
Yeah, the White House
overruled the CDC

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:00.019
on the current cruise ship ban,

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:02.721
which might explain
this new ad I saw.

00:07:02.721 --> 00:07:04.556
-Are you ready to get out
of your apartment?

00:07:04.556 --> 00:07:06.259
-Yes.
-Are you tired of your

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:08.961
same old pandemic routine?
-Oh, yeah.

00:07:08.961 --> 00:07:12.531
-Then join us this November
for a Carnival Cruise.

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:14.800
[ Ship horn blows ]
-Wait, what?

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.903
-Dive into a pool filled with
kids swimming in diapers.

00:07:17.903 --> 00:07:20.039
-Do I have to?
-Share a wet mic

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:22.407
at a karaoke lounge.
-Why?

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:25.177
-Dig in hands first
at our delicious buffet.

00:07:25.177 --> 00:07:27.179
-Is this a trap?
-Carnival Cruise.

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:30.182 line:0%
Just a few liability waivers
away from setting sail.

00:07:30.182 --> 00:07:31.750 line:0%
[ Ship horn blows ]

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:32.919
[ Imitates horn ]

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.753
[ Applause ]

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:36.122
Well, this isn't good.

00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.589
The highest court in Ireland

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:39.925
just made a pretty shocking
ruling, listen to this.

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:42.394
-Ireland Supreme Court has
ruled that the bread served

00:07:42.394 --> 00:07:46.432
at Subway restaurants can't
legally be defined as bread.

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:48.667
Subway's bread contains
five times

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:51.603
the qualifying limit of sugar.

00:07:51.603 --> 00:07:53.839
-Man, all this time
I thought it was healthy

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:56.609
to eat a meatball parm
on 12 inches of honey bread.

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:58.143
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.143 --> 00:08:00.412
Why am I gaining weight?

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:02.648
After the ruling,
Subway was like, "Whew.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.583
They didn't say anything
about the meat."

00:08:04.583 --> 00:08:07.486
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.454
It wasn't just bread.
The court also said,

00:08:09.454 --> 00:08:11.757
"And by the way, stop calling
the guy making my sandwich

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:14.760
an 'artist.'"
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.996
That wasn't true.
I made that up. That was a joke.

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:19.232
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.833
Also, what's going on in Ireland

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.301
where that made it to their
highest court?

00:08:23.301 --> 00:08:26.071
Our highest court is about
to argue over health care,

00:08:26.071 --> 00:08:28.874
and Ireland's arguing
over sandwiches.

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:31.577
Can we live there?
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:32.945
Then the justices are like,

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:34.379
[ Irish accent ]
"Next on the docket,

00:08:34.379 --> 00:08:37.450
are Taco Bell's tacos
actually tacos?"

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.953
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:43.322
That's one of my Irish accents,
but this --

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:46.625
This one, what I do, it's
the out-of-breath Irish accent.

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:48.393
Can you do an Irish accent?
-Sure.

00:08:48.393 --> 00:08:51.330
-Do it.
Say "Taco Bell's aren't tacos."

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.665
-[ Irish accent ]
Taco Bell's aren't tacos!

00:08:53.665 --> 00:08:58.737
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:58.737 --> 00:09:00.706
-That's not Irish. I don't know
who you sound like,

00:09:00.706 --> 00:09:02.007
but it's not Irish, but --

00:09:02.007 --> 00:09:05.077
But now do it but run out
of breath, like...

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:07.380
-Okay. Uh, tacos...

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.181
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:11.884
-I'm not a --
I'm not a dialect coach.

00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:14.653
What am I -- what am I doing?
What am I doing?

00:09:14.653 --> 00:09:16.088
I apologize. I apologize.

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:20.426
-Your Irish accent sounds
more Jamaican to me.

00:09:20.426 --> 00:09:22.194
-[ Irish accent ]
"You never go to Jamaica...

00:09:22.194 --> 00:09:24.129
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:09:24.129 --> 00:09:26.866
...get jerk chicken."
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:28.868
"They serve real
jerk chicken there!"

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:29.902
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:31.570
-I love it. Ole.

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:35.707
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:35.707 --> 00:09:38.410
-I saw that a company
in the UK is testing a new way

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.512
to speed up paramedics'
response time.

00:09:40.512 --> 00:09:41.913
This is cool, watch this.

00:09:41.913 --> 00:09:43.348 line:0%
-You could be looking at
the future

00:09:43.348 --> 00:09:46.052
of emergency aid in this
simulation from the UK.

00:09:46.052 --> 00:09:47.553
The paramedic with the
medical kit could

00:09:47.553 --> 00:09:50.289
quickly respond to people
in a jet pack.

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:54.393
The suit has two mini engines on
each arm and one on the back.

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:56.228
[ Laughter ]

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:57.463
-Right now that guy is
currently hovering

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:58.931
over 50 Carnival Cruise ships.

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:02.334
[ Laughter ]

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:03.703
Yeah, it's "quick."

00:10:03.703 --> 00:10:06.271
All paramedics have to do
is get in the suit,

00:10:06.271 --> 00:10:07.639
put on the gloves
and the helmet,

00:10:07.639 --> 00:10:09.741
strap on the jet pack,
make sure he has enough fuel,

00:10:09.741 --> 00:10:11.543
walk out to an open field,
take off

00:10:11.543 --> 00:10:13.545
and slowly fly their way over.

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:15.714
And don't worry, there's
also a second paramedic

00:10:15.714 --> 00:10:18.250
traveling behind for when
the first paramedic crashes.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.718
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.718 --> 00:10:21.620
I'm just messing with you.
If there's one thing we know,

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.054
jet suits never fail.

00:10:23.054 --> 00:10:24.890
-And it starts right now.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.994
-Oh! Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:10:27.994 --> 00:10:30.262
-Classic. Pulling out
the classic, man.

